  message: "Done in PR #2337 (dev fcad17866 for the rows; 351c6aa6f, a037577a4, 0dc5aea71 for the three changes they stand on).\n\nTHE FILED REPRO, RE-RUN on dev a89850612 (fixture ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/rasok_11222026/fixtures/methfx, hypergumbo run, then read the nodes): Python TestMath.test_adds -> test_function; ThingsResource.on_get / on_post -> route_handler (falcon.yaml); Ruby MathTest#test_adds -> test_function; Swift XTests.testAdds -> test_function, XTests.setUp -> test_lifecycle; Groovy MathSpec.setup -> test_lifecycle; Scala MathSuite.test -> nothing (by decision, below); the Spock feature method def \"should add\"() is still not a symbol. swift-argument-parser: 556 methods whose own name starts with test, 556 with test_function (0 before).\n\nWHAT WAS DONE AGAINST THE ASK. (1) method_name reads the member's own name through member_names (every owner separator) and symbol_kind / framework_role / meta_match bind every match type. (2) The item's list has 18 rows, not 17. 13 are moved to method_name: the eight responder rows, Python, Ruby test_, Swift x2, Groovy fixture methods. (3) Each test row asks for a FILE, and only for paths paths.is_test_file accepts (a test function the ranking does not demote would lead the entry list). (4) A/B, one run per arm on 26 trees: declared symbols gone 0, stable ids moved 0; test_function +2,187 (Python 1,001, Ruby 156, Swift 1,030), test_lifecycle +86, test_function -157 (156 helpers nested in Python tests, one Scala example helper); entry lists unchanged but for that Scala entry. 29 mutation controls red.\n\nNOT ASSERTED / NOT DONE, each filed:\n- 2 Scala name rows DELETED, not moved: of 111 test-named methods in tapir none is a test (my decision; say if you want them back).\n- 3 rows still match nothing because their test is a CALL, not a symbol (RSpec it / describe, the Spock feature row): marked NOT A SYMBOL. WI-tavum.\n- Other name-only test rows still mark production code: WI-zofob. EUnit rows left unrepaired and why: WI-potol (needs a ruling). Kotlin parent_base_class: WI-marun. Groovy lost class: WI-goduz. is_test_file gaps: WI-gunaf. Fallback picks: WI-lunul. Instance/class dispatch: WI-fupaj. Separator inside a member name: WI-zojun.\n- The responder rows were measured on a fixture only (no repository of that framework on this machine).\nAlso fixed on the way: Ruby class methods of namespaced classes were split at the namespace (chatwoot: 159 contains edges re-parented); the connectivity fallback did not fire when only test entries were detected. WI-jakiv (the ignored symbol_kind) is closed by the same PR.\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/rasok_11222026/RESULTS.md."  # 9df3
